diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 60bb229..2b4352c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,5 +1,30 @@
-# Academic Research Profile Website
+# Alexis Grédelue — Machine Learning Engineer
 
-A clean, maintainable academic personal website for presenting an early-career research profile at the intersection of computational physics, statistical learning, particle physics, cosmology, and scientific computing.
+Personal portfolio website: machine-learning projects, experience and skills.
 
-The site is intentionally designed as an academic homepage for prospective PhD supervisors and committees.
+**Live site:** https://alexis744.github.io/ai-engineer/
+
+## Highlights
+
+- ML surrogate models for the CERN ATLAS Collaboration: Random Forest, Neural Network and XGBoost benchmarked on 1M+ simulated events; final XGBoost model of 1.44 MB with a +0.01% net yield bias on a 349k-event held-out set.
+- Engineering degree in Physics, MSc Universe & Particles, University Diploma in Data Science.
+
+## Structure
+
+```
+index.html            Page layout
+assets/js/data.js     All page content (edit text here)
+assets/js/main.js     Rendering entry point
+assets/css/styles.css Styles
+assets/docs/          CV and technical report
+scripts/build.js      Static build to dist/
+```
+
+## Local development
+
+```bash
+npm run build      # copies the site to dist/
+npm run serve      # serves the site locally
+```
+
+Deployment to GitHub Pages runs automatically on every push to `main` (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`).
diff --git a/assets/css/styles.css b/assets/css/styles.css
index 61cd137..663b92b 100644
--- a/assets/css/styles.css
+++ b/assets/css/styles.css
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 /*
-  Academic GitHub Pages website stylesheet.
+  Personal website stylesheet.
 */
 
 :root {
@@ -217,7 +217,7 @@ p { margin: 0; } p + p { margin-top: 1.1rem; }
 }
 
 
-/* Evidence-first academic homepage additions */
+/* Homepage components */
 .evidence-panel,
 .fit-panel,
 .cv-panel {
@@ -450,8 +450,8 @@ p { margin: 0; } p + p { margin-top: 1.1rem; }
 }
 
 
-/* Academic convention adjustments from 50-site audit */
-.academic-profile {
+/* Profile layout */
+.profile-layout {
   display: grid;
   grid-template-columns: minmax(210px, .42fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(280px, .62fr);
   gap: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 3rem);
@@ -564,7 +564,7 @@ p { margin: 0; } p + p { margin-top: 1.1rem; }
 }
 
 @media (max-width: 1120px) {
-  .academic-profile {
+  .profile-layout {
     grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(280px, .8fr);
   }
   .profile-card {
@@ -679,7 +679,7 @@ p { margin: 0; } p + p { margin-top: 1.1rem; }
 }
 
 @media (max-width: 980px) {
-  .academic-profile,
+  .profile-layout,
   .profile-card {
     grid-template-columns: 1fr;
   }
